{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:23.385186+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"Thanks for the report! I think the issue is that pickle always places the loaded array on the default device. You'll have to re-replicate your array in the third case if you want it to be identical to the first two cases.\r\n\r\nSee https://jax.readthedocs.io/en/latest/jax.numpy.html#copying-and-serialization for details.","created_at":"2023-11-21T20:52:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617#issuecomment-1821661681","id":1821661681,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5slFnx","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1821661681/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-11-21T20:52:46Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1821661681","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","id":781659,"login":"jakevdp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"In this case there is only a single device, so the new X should be default-committed there. I have also tried fixing it further by including the line `X = jax.device_put(X, jax.local_devices()[0])` after `print('Loaded X')`, but to no avail.","created_at":"2023-11-22T06:48:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617#issuecomment-1822203776","id":1822203776,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5snJ-A","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1822203776/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-11-22T06:48:20Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1822203776","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10989937?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jbuckman","id":10989937,"login":"jbuckman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTg5OTM3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman","user_view_type":"public"}},{"author_association":"NONE","body":"I found a workaround. Manually removing the extra dimension on the arrays before saving (which I am forced to do on CPU since we cannot donate buffers when reshaping), and then re-invoking `device_put_replicated` after loading, leads to buffers being donated correctly. I guess `device_put_replicated` is doing something important under the hood besides changing the shape and committing to a device.\r\n\r\n```python\r\n@jax.jit\r\ndef unpack(pt):\r\n    return jax.tree_map(lambda arr: arr[0], pt)\r\n\r\n# This is the function I want to call\r\ndef add1(s):\r\n    return jax.tree_map(lambda x: x + 1, s)\r\n\r\n# This is the input. Adjust the size based on your GPU.\r\n# This number is for an A6000 with XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_MEM_FRACTION=1.\r\nGIANT_ARRAY_SIZE = 6750078228\r\nX = {'w': jnp.arange(GIANT_ARRAY_SIZE, dtype=jnp.float32)}\r\njax.device_put_replicated(X, jax.local_devices())\r\njax.block_until_ready(X)\r\nprint('Created X')\r\n\r\npath = '/tmp/test.pkl'\r\nif os.path.exists(path):\r\n    os.remove(path)\r\nwith open(path, 'wb') as file:\r\n    pickle.dump(unpack(jax.device_put(X, jax.devices('cpu')[0])), file)\r\nprint('Dumped X')\r\ndel X\r\nprint('Deleted X')\r\nwith open(path, 'rb') as file:\r\n    X = pickle.load(file)\r\nprint('Loaded X')\r\n\r\nX = jax.device_put_replicated(X, jax.local_devices())\r\njax.block_until_ready(X)\r\nprint('Put X onto GPU')\r\np_add1 = jax.pmap(add1, axis_name='data_parallel', donate_argnums=0)\r\nX = p_add1(X)\r\n```","created_at":"2023-11-25T13:59:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617#issuecomment-1826328186","id":1826328186,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5s2456","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1826328186/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-11-25T13:59:18Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1826328186","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10989937?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jbuckman","id":10989937,"login":"jbuckman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTg5OTM3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","id":781659,"login":"jakevdp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","user_view_type":"public"},"assignees":[{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jakevdp","id":781659,"login":"jakevdp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4MTY1OQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp","user_view_type":"public"}],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Description\r\n\r\nI've found what I suspect to be a bug in donating buffers. Create an array that is small enough that it fits in memory, but large enough that it does *not* fit in memory twice. Calling a simple pmapped function with a correctly-set `donate_buffers` should work, since the large array is never in memory twice. This works if we create the array directly, but fails if we create the array via a load from disk using `pickle`.\r\n\r\nThe code to reproduce is below. Set the `GIANT_ARRAY_SIZE` to an appropriate size such that setting `WHICH=1` fails but `WHICH=2` succeeds, and you will see that `WHICH=3` fails (it should succeed).\r\n\r\n```python\r\nimport pickle\r\nimport jax\r\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\r\n\r\n# This is the function I want to call\r\ndef add1(s):\r\n    return jax.tree_map(lambda x: x + 1, s)\r\n\r\n# This is the input. Adjust the size based on your GPU.\r\n# This number is for an H100 with XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_MEM_FRACTION=1.\r\nGIANT_ARRAY_SIZE = 9750078228\r\nX = {'w': jnp.arange(GIANT_ARRAY_SIZE, dtype=jnp.float32)}\r\nX = jax.device_put_replicated(X, jax.local_devices())\r\njax.block_until_ready(X)\r\nprint('Created X')\r\n\r\nWHICH = 1\r\nprint('Running', WHICH)\r\n# V1: call without donated buffer\r\nif WHICH == 1:\r\n    p_add1 = jax.pmap(add1, axis_name='data_parallel')\r\n    X = p_add1(X) # crashes OOM\r\n\r\n# V2: call with donated buffer\r\nelif WHICH == 2:\r\n    p_add1 = jax.pmap(add1, axis_name='data_parallel', donate_argnums=0)\r\n    X = p_add1(X)  # succeeds\r\n\r\n# V3: call with donated buffer after loading from pickle\r\nelse:\r\n    path = '/tmp/test.pkl'\r\n    with open(path, 'wb') as file:\r\n        pickle.dump(X, file)\r\n    print('Dumped X')\r\n    del X\r\n    print('Deleted X')\r\n    with open(path, 'rb') as file:\r\n        X = pickle.load(file)\r\n    print('Loaded X')\r\n\r\n    p_add1 = jax.pmap(add1, axis_name='data_parallel', donate_argnums=0)\r\n    X = p_add1(X) # crashes OOM\r\n\r\njax.block_until_ready(X)\r\nprint('Finished')\r\n```\r\n\r\n### What jax/jaxlib version are you using?\r\n\r\njax v0.4.20, jaxlib v0.4.20\r\n\r\n### Which accelerator(s) are you using?\r\n\r\nGPU\r\n\r\n### Additional system info\r\n\r\nPython 311, Ubuntu 22.04\r\n\r\n### NVIDIA GPU info\r\n\r\n```\r\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\r\n| NVIDIA-SMI 535.129.03             Driver Version: 535.129.03   CUDA Version: 12.2     |\r\n|-----------------------------------------+----------------------+----------------------+\r\n| GPU  Name                 Persistence-M | Bus-Id        Disp.A | Volatile Uncorr. ECC |\r\n| Fan  Temp   Perf          Pwr:Usage/Cap |         Memory-Usage | GPU-Util  Compute M. |\r\n|                                         |                      |               MIG M. |\r\n|=========================================+======================+======================|\r\n|   0  NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3          On  | 00000000:04:00.0 Off |                  Off |\r\n| N/A   38C    P0             113W / 700W |   1332MiB / 81559MiB |      0%      Default |\r\n|                                         |                      |             Disabled |\r\n+-----------------------------------------+----------------------+----------------------+\r\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\r\n| Processes:                                                                            |\r\n|  GPU   GI   CI        PID   Type   Process name                            GPU Memory |\r\n|        ID   ID                                                             Usage      |\r\n|=======================================================================================|\r\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\r\n```","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":3,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617/comments","created_at":"2023-11-21T06:16:27Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617","id":2003540591,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","id":1104782284,"name":"bug","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTA0NzgyMjg0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/labels/bug"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"I_kwDOCTkjjc53a5pv","number":18617,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pinned_comment":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax","state":"open","state_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"completed":0,"percent_completed":0,"total":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/186