_via_github_app":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/events/11029118609"},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10989937?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jbuckman","id":10989937,"login":"jbuckman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTg5OTM3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"NONE","body":"In this case there is only a single device, so the new X should be default-committed there. I have also tried fixing it further by including the line `X = jax.device_put(X, jax.local_devices()[0])` after `print('Loaded X')`, but to no avail.","created_at":"2023-11-22T06:48:20Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617#issuecomment-1822203776","id":1822203776,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5snJ-A","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1822203776/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-11-22T06:48:20Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1822203776","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10989937?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jbuckman","id":10989937,"login":"jbuckman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTg5OTM3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman","user_view_type":"public"}},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10989937?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jbuckman","id":10989937,"login":"jbuckman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTg5OTM3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman","user_view_type":"public"},"author_association":"NONE","body":"I found a workaround. Manually removing the extra dimension on the arrays before saving (which I am forced to do on CPU since we cannot donate buffers when reshaping), and then re-invoking `device_put_replicated` after loading, leads to buffers being donated correctly. I guess `device_put_replicated` is doing something important under the hood besides changing the shape and committing to a device.\r\n\r\n```python\r\n@jax.jit\r\ndef unpack(pt):\r\n    return jax.tree_map(lambda arr: arr[0], pt)\r\n\r\n# This is the function I want to call\r\ndef add1(s):\r\n    return jax.tree_map(lambda x: x + 1, s)\r\n\r\n# This is the input. Adjust the size based on your GPU.\r\n# This number is for an A6000 with XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_MEM_FRACTION=1.\r\nGIANT_ARRAY_SIZE = 6750078228\r\nX = {'w': jnp.arange(GIANT_ARRAY_SIZE, dtype=jnp.float32)}\r\njax.device_put_replicated(X, jax.local_devices())\r\njax.block_until_ready(X)\r\nprint('Created X')\r\n\r\npath = '/tmp/test.pkl'\r\nif os.path.exists(path):\r\n    os.remove(path)\r\nwith open(path, 'wb') as file:\r\n    pickle.dump(unpack(jax.device_put(X, jax.devices('cpu')[0])), file)\r\nprint('Dumped X')\r\ndel X\r\nprint('Deleted X')\r\nwith open(path, 'rb') as file:\r\n    X = pickle.load(file)\r\nprint('Loaded X')\r\n\r\nX = jax.device_put_replicated(X, jax.local_devices())\r\njax.block_until_ready(X)\r\nprint('Put X onto GPU')\r\np_add1 = jax.pmap(add1, axis_name='data_parallel', donate_argnums=0)\r\nX = p_add1(X)\r\n```","created_at":"2023-11-25T13:59:18Z","event":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617#issuecomment-1826328186","id":1826328186,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc5s2456","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1826328186/reactions"},"updated_at":"2023-11-25T13:59:18Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/1826328186","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10989937?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jbuckman","id":10989937,"login":"jbuckman","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTg5OTM3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jbuckman","user_view_type":"public"}},{"actor":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246472660?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ocg-goodfire/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ocg-goodfire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ocg-goodfire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ocg-goodfire/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ocg-goodfire","id":246472660,"login":"ocg-goodfire","node_id":"U_kgDODrDf1A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ocg-goodfire/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ocg-goodfire/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ocg-goodfire/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ocg-goodfire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ocg-goodfire/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ocg-goodfire","user_view_type":"public"},"created_at":"2026-07-03T11:58:00Z","event":"cross-referenced","source":{"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"## Description\nThree commits:\n\n1. **`restore_step` re-materialises the restored tree as jit outputs** (non-donating identity jit pinned to `reference.format` via `out_shardings`), replacing the `device_put(format)` coercion. Orbax-restored arrays (per-shard `device_put` + `make_array_from_single_device_arrays`) are not reliably donatable to the jitted train step ([jax#18617](https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617), never fixed upstream). When dispatch-time donation fails it is **silent** (the `Some donated buffers were not usable` warning is lowering-time only — `jax/_src/interpreters/mlir.py`), and the first resumed step peaks ~one full `TrainState` above any fresh step: the full32L resume OOM (lore `2026-07-03--resume-oom-is-buffer-donation-asymmetry`). Jit outputs are indistinguishable from fresh-init state; the transient 2×-state cost equals the peak restore already paid while `reference` and the restored tree coexisted. Non-donating deliberately: a plain copy cannot hard-fail at dispatch (GPU errors loudly on donation of externally-referenced buffers), and the reuse donation would buy is off the step's peak. Covers the fine-tune path too (`init_from_parent` → `restore_step`).\n   Plus a **bytes-weighted buffer-reuse guard** after the first resumed step (`run.py`): if <95% of state bytes were reused, each affected rank prints `DONATION FAILED …` — the silent failure mode is silent no more.\n\n2. **`invariance_check.py` fed float residuals** where the target now takes token ids (same fallout class as #919) — validation-stack item 3 was unrunnable. Now feeds `randint` tokens.\n\n3. **dp8 save→resume smoke config** documenting the scancel-after-save → `pd-lm --run_id` resubmit procedure.\n\n## Related Issue\nBridge task `solve-resumption-oom`; upstream [jax#18617](https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/18617).\n\n## Motivation and Context\nLarge-state donating runs can train fresh but die on any preemption/requeue: full32L resumes OOM'd at the default mem fraction, and for `p-8e2380e2` (attn C=4096) the mem-fraction band-aid is unusable in both directions (0.97 starves NCCL clique init; even max fraction cannot fit fresh-peak + one state). The restored state must donate.\n\n## How Has This Been Tested?\n- **Repro harness** (task workspace `repro/repro_donation.py`): orbax StandardSave/Restore + donating jitted step, donation observed directly via per-shard `unsafe_buffer_pointer` aliasing + `memory_stats`. On CPU, raw restored state flakily fails donation on a random subset of leaves — exclusively the *sharded* ones; the identity-jit re-materialisation fixes it deterministically. (GPU 1-dev and 8-proc×1-GPU multi-controller runs did not reproduce the raw failure at small scale — 48/48 rank×mode combos aliased — so CPU + the at-scale diag logs are the only places the failure is visible; the fix makes the restored arrays *constructively* equivalent to fresh-init ones rather than relying on that.)\n- `test_checkpoint.py::test_restored_state_is_donatable` pins the contract (pointer aliasing through a donating jit); ran 3× stable at 4 sim devices.\n- Full `param_decomp/tests/` green at default device count AND `--xla_force_host_platform_device_count=4`; `make type` clean; `invariance_check.py` passes at 4 sim devices (worst rel 1.02e-04).\n- **End-to-end dp8 trainer smoke** (LlamaSimpleMLP pile, scavenge jobs 170727/170729): fresh run → scancel → SIGTERM save at step 70 → `pd-lm --run_id` resubmit → `resumed from checkpoint step 70`, first resumed step trains, **no DONATION FAILED line from any rank**, losses continue the trajectory, per-rank peak identical (18.22 GB). Run + workspaces deleted after.\n- NOT yet validated at 128-proc scale (the original OOM artifact `p-05101e15` was GC'd; `p-8e2380e2` is live). The guard turns any residual at-scale failure loud on the next real resume.\n\n## Does this PR introduce a breaking change?\nNo. `restore_step` now requires the reference on a single device set (one jit over the tree) — production references already are (`_ensure_global`); the sharded test fixture was aligned to that contract.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","closed_at":"2026-07-24T15:59:11Z","comments":0,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodfire-ai/param-decomp/issues/932/comments","created_at":"2026-07-03T11:57:59Z","draft":false,"events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodfire-ai/param-decomp/issues/932/events","html_url":"https://github.com/goodfire-ai/param-decomp/pull/932","id":4803242583,"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodfire-ai/param-decomp/issues/932/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"PR_kwDOO5xtfc7tktGq","number":932,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pull_request":{"diff_url":"https://github.com/goodfire-ai/param-decomp/pull/932.diff","html_url":"https://github.com/goodfire-ai/param-decomp/pull/932","merged_at":null,"patch_url":"https://github.com/goodfire-ai/param-decomp/pull/932.patch","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodfire-ai/param-decomp/pulls/932"},"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodfire-ai/param-decomp/issues/932/reactions"},"repository":{"allow_forking":true,"archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodfire-ai/param-decomp/{archive_format}{/ref}","archived":false,"assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodfire-ai/param-decomp/assignees{/user}","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodfire-ai/param-decomp/git/blobs{/sha}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodfire-ai/param-decomp/branches{/branch}","clone_url":"https://github.com/goodfire-ai/param-decomp.git","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodfire-ai/param-decomp/collaborators{/collaborator}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/goodfire-ai/param-decomp/comments{/numbe